/393.added.md", "line": 5, "text": "field, such as row counts, sizes, defaults, comments and constraint names, comes"}, {"file": "docs/external/rule-sets.md", "line": 122, "text": "To look up the schema, the assistant can read `information_schema.TABLES`, `COLUMNS` and `KEY_COLUMN_USAGE`. Under a rule set these show only the selected set's"}, {"file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/rule-sets.md", "line": 57, "text": "- Passes `rule_sets=True` to `DefaultSystemPromptBuilder`, which adds a rule to correct and rerun a query refused with `Refused by the rule set:`, and, when a d"}, {"file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/rule-sets.md", "line": 62, "text": "`RuleSetGuardRunner` (`src/sqllens/safety/rule_sets.py`) parses each statement with sqlglot under the MySQL dialect and refuses anything it cannot carry through"}, {"file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/rule-sets.md", "line": 64, "text": "A reference to `information_schema.TABLES`, `COLUMNS` or `KEY_COLUMN_USAGE`, in any letter case, becomes a derived table over that view (`_catalog_body`). It ke"}, {"file": "src/sqllens/agent/core/system_prompt/default.py", "line": 63, "text": "a dialect resolves, a database rule to qualify every column,"}, {"file": "src/sqllens/agent/core/system_prompt/default.py", "line": 67, "text": "``base_prompt`` is returned as given, so none of these changes"}, {"file": "src/sqllens/agent/core/system_prompt/default.py", "line": 191, "text": "# every other catalog read and every SHOW statement."}, {"file": "src/sqllens/safety/rule_sets.py", "line": 24, "text": "columns), projects every field of the view under its"}, {"file": "src/sqllens/safety/rule_sets.py", "line": 27, "text": "read it. Every other catalog relation is refused."}, {"file": "src/sqllens/safety/rule_sets.py", "line": 95, "text": "\"\"\"A rewritten ``information_schema`` view: every field in view order, and the kept ones.\"\"\""}, {"file": "src/sqllens/safety/rule_sets.py", "line": 100, "text": "def __post_init__(self) -> None:"}, {"file": "src/sqllens/safety/rule_sets.py", "line": 101, "text": "if not self.fields or len(set(self.fields)) != len(self.fields):"}, {"file": "src/sqllens/safety/rule_sets.py", "line": 108, "text": "# missing here would disappear from ``SELECT *``; a field added to ``kept``"}, {"file": "tests/connectors/test_rule_sets_mysql.py", "line": 83, "text": "# rs_orders.discount references rs_customers: KEY_COLUMN_USAGE must hide both."}, {"file": "tests/connectors/test_rule_sets_mysql.py", "line": 85, "text": "\" email VARCHAR(80), rep_id INT, account_id INT,\""}, {"file": "tests/connectors/test_rule_sets_mysql.py", "line": 88, "text": "\" discount INT, account_id INT,\""}, {"file": "tests/connectors/test_rule_sets_mysql.py", "line": 158, "text": "for statement in [*_SETUP, *(_other_setup(other) if other else [])]:"}, {"file": "tests/connectors/test_rule_sets_mysql.py", "line": 164, "text": "for statement in _TEARDOWN:"}, {"file": "tests/connectors/test_rule_sets_mysql.py", "line": 573, "text": "tuple(None if pd.isna(v) else v for v in row) for row in frame.values.tolist()"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_factory_wiring.py", "line": 753, "text": ") -> None:"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_factory_wiring.py", "line": 767, "text": "added = [d[2:] for d in diff if d.startswith(\"+ \")]"}, {"file": "tests/unit/test_factory_wiring.py", "line": 768, "text": "removed = [d[2:] for d in diff if d.startswith(\"- \")]"}], "audit_hints_truncated": true, "views": {"head": {"dir": ".prflow/tmp/review/pr-393/43589367319-1/view-head", "revision": "4498342716a0a2547b622d90291217bc270b90ff"}, "base": {"dir": ".prflow/tmp/review/pr-393/43589367319-1/view-base", "revision": "49bb9700167ec9d2da375c7c8937afa6bad0de98"}}, "pr": {"number": "393", "body": ".prflow/tmp/review/pr-393/43589367319-1/pr-body.md", "head_ref": "issue-379-per-role-rule-sets-part-1b-mysql-rewrite-catalog", "base_ref": "main", "api_head_sha": "4498342716a0a2547b622d90291217bc270b90ff", "author_trust": "not-looked-up